Scrum Board Progress Explanation

The three images provided show the progression of our Scrum board throughout the sprint.

In the first image (start.png), the board is mostly empty, with user stories still in the “To Do” column and no tasks actively being worked on. This represents the initial state before any work has begun.

In the second image (middle.png), all group members’ user stories have been added to the board. At this stage, I moved my own user story from the “To Do” column into the “In Progress” column, indicating that I had started working on it.

In the final image (end.png), my user story has been completed and moved into the “Done” column. After finishing my task, I then moved the next person’s user story into the “In Progress” column, showing a continuation of workflow within the team.

Overall, these images demonstrate the progression of tasks across the Scrum board, from initial planning, to active development, and finally to completion.